# A `match` with no arm is exhaustive over a choice with no case and over nothing else
# (hosting bug 29: `type Never = choice:` and `fn Absurd never = match never:` are legal;
# Type System ch. 2, "Patterns and exhaustiveness": a match covers every value of its
# type). `Bool` has two values, so the empty `match` misses one.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*

Wrong: fn Bool -> Nat
fn Wrong flag = match flag:

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Wrong True}")
